              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the French for the possibility, then the French for for lack of."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: l'imprévu",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "l'imprévu — \"the hitch, the unexpected event\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "J'ai un imprévu, je ne peux pas venir ce soir. Something has come up, I cannot come tonight."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Also an adjective: une visite imprévue. Masculine."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "imprévu is built from in- \"not\" and prévu, the participle of prévoir \"to foresee\" (EtymDB), from Latin praevidēre \"to foresee\", built on vidēre \"to see\" (Lewis & Short)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for telling, explaining and describing at B1."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
